Consumer demand for recycled content products requires transparent communication about actual recycled material percentages. Visible labelling overcomes perception gaps where consumers cannot distinguish recycled-content from virgin-material products. Clear labelling builds brand differentiation for manufacturers pursuing secondary material strategies.

Transparent recycled content communication prevents greenwashing accusations and builds consumer trust. Standardized labelling enables fair comparison across products and manufacturers. Visible recycled content information appeals to environmentally conscious consumers influencing purchasing decisions.